text:
mark the words allows you to write a sentence and have user select individual as solutions question. marked well those not are able give feedback per answer if desired.
example

developer
npm install @haxtheweb/mark-the-words --savesource on githubcodepen example from cdn

&lt;mark-the-words question="select all of contractions" statement="i been farm-house, however; itll be fun attend!"&gt;
  &lt;input type="checkbox" value="it'll" correct="correct" data-selected="you correct" role="textbox"&gt;
 value="attend!" data-selected="hey, ! is for "&gt;
&lt;/mark-the-words&gt;

matching question, often called a drag and drop, allows for setting drop targets to possible answers. can have multiple answers associated with them there also be options that no target. correctness is visualized on the in context.
example

developer
npm install @haxtheweb/matching-question --savesource githubcodepen example from cdn

&lt;matching-question question="what does animal say?" data-accent="2" max-attempts="0" typeof="oer:assessment" resource="#1377c130-1d8e-6a7c-33bf-2b09c5b89fe2" prefix="oer:http://oerschema.org/ schema:http://schema.org/ dc:http://purl.org/dc/terms/ foaf:http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/ cc:http://creativecommons.org/ns# bib:http://bib.schema.org " quiz-name="default"&gt;
  &lt;input type="checkbox" value="cow" correct="correct" role="textbox"&gt;
 value="moo"&gt;
 value="fox" correct="correct"&gt;
 value="papapower"&gt;
 value="haykeewell"&gt;
&lt;/matching-question&gt;

when reading content or processing a lecture, its good idea to stop and ask the user questions about what they experienced. multiple choice are simple comprehension check. note that data is not stored sent anywhere, for time being this just checking ones understanding.
example



video


developers
npm install @haxtheweb/multiple-choice --savesource on githubcodepen example from cdn

&lt;multiple-choice randomize="" typeof="oer:assessment" resource="#6400762a-2b00-60d6-9410-db72d033c61a" prefix="oer:http://oerschema.org/ schema:http://schema.org/ dc:http://purl.org/dc/terms/ foaf:http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/ cc:http://creativecommons.org/ns# bib:http://bib.schema.org " correct-text="let's go vgk!" incorrect-text="nooooooo!!!" check-label="check answer" reset-label="reset" correct-icon="icons:thumb-up" incorrect-icon="icons:thumb-down" quiz-name="default" question="who last won nhl stanley cup?" single-option="" max-attempts="0"&gt;
  &lt;input type="checkbox" value="seattle kraken" role="textbox"&gt;
 value="vegas golden knights"&gt;
 value="florida panthers" correct="correct"&gt;
 value="edmonton oilers"&gt;
&lt;/multiple-choice&gt;

short answer supports multiple possible answers and is best utilized with single words for accuracy in user entry.
example

developer
npm install @haxtheweb/multiple-choice --save (short-answer-question included this package)source on githubcodepen example from cdn

&lt;short-answer-question question="which direction a compass rose always pointing up?" max-attempts="0" typeof="oer:assessment" resource="#438bb5f5-42fc-c5d7-b6c1-80de2a8efbc9" prefix="oer:http://oerschema.org/ schema:http://schema.org/ dc:http://purl.org/dc/terms/ foaf:http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/ cc:http://creativecommons.org/ns# bib:http://bib.schema.org " quiz-name="default" single-option=""&gt;
  &lt;input type="checkbox" value="north" correct="correct" role="textbox"&gt;
&lt;/short-answer-question&gt;

sorting questions can be used to make users place items in the correct order. results are randomized and user try it again with feedback on which incorrect shown sort options themselves.
example
self evident, refer back 1st gradeconsider that numbers tend go zero, one, two...
developers
npm install @haxtheweb/sorting-questionsource githubcodepen sample via cdn

&lt;sorting-question question="sorting these numerical order" randomize=""&gt;
  &lt;p slot="evidence"&gt;self grade&lt;/p&gt;
 slot="hint"&gt;consider two...&lt;/p&gt;
 &lt;input type="checkbox" value="roaring 20s" role="textbox"&gt;
 value="1980s - strange...things.."&gt;
 value="the year 2000"&gt;
&lt;/sorting-question&gt;

tagging questions allow for a drag and drop or click to select method of answering.
  they you add options that are incorrect the user must only&nbsp;select
 correct answers without selecting any ones.
example

developers

 npm install @haxtheweb/tagging-question --save
 source on github
 codepen
 example from cdn



&lt;tagging-question question="what does fox say?" data-primary="15"&gt;
 &lt;input type="checkbox" value="dingdingding" correct="correct"&gt;
 value="papapower" value="moo"&gt;
&lt;/tagging-question&gt;

